.\" FreeBASIC NuttX SDK
.\" -------------------
.\" File: fbc-nuttx-esp32p4.1
.\" Purpose: Document the installed ESP32-P4 application build and upload driver.
.\" Responsibilities: Describe the normal build, transfer, and run workflow.
.\" This file intentionally does not document NuttX firmware construction.
.\"
.TH FBC-NUTTX-ESP32P4 1 "2026-07-30" "FreeBASIC NuttX SDK" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fbc-nuttx-esp32p4 \- build and deploy a FreeBASIC NuttX module for ESP32-P4
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbc-nuttx-esp32p4
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbc-nuttx-esp32p4
generates C from a FreeBASIC program, builds it as a loadable NuttX RISC-V
module, and can transfer the module and data files to an ESP32-P4 board.
The first normal run prepares a NuttX workspace when one is not already
available. Firmware flashing is handled by
.BR fbc-nuttx-esp32p4-firmware (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --nuttx-workdir " DIR"
Use the workspace containing the NuttX and apps source trees.
.TP
.BI --bas " FILE"
Build the specified FreeBASIC source file.
.TP
.BI --app-name " NAME"
Set the NuttX module name.
.TP
.BI --generated-c " FILE"
Compile existing generated C instead of invoking the FreeBASIC compiler.
.TP
.B --with-gfxlib
Link the NuttX graphics support objects.
.TP
.B --sfx-no-media-decoders
Link generated-tone sound support without the media decoders.
.TP
.BI --asset " FILE[:DEST]"
Transfer an additional data file. The option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR --storage " " data | sd | auto
Select the board storage root. The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI --board-ip " ADDRESS"
Use the given board address for telnet control.
.TP
.BI --serial-port " DEVICE"
Use a serial console for first-contact address discovery and control.
.TP
.BR --control " " auto | telnet | serial | none
Select the board control transport.
.TP
.B --run
Run the uploaded module after transfer.
.TP
.B --no-upload
Build and stage the module without contacting a board.
.TP
.B --prepare-only
Prepare the workspace, then stop.
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete option and environment reference.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NUTTX_WORKDIR, FB_NUTTX_ESP32P4_WORKDIR
Default NuttX workspace.
.TP
.B FBC
FreeBASIC compiler used to generate C.
.TP
.B FB_NUTTX_BOARD_IP
Default ESP32-P4 board address.
.TP
.B ESPTOOL_PORT
Default serial device.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbc (1),
.BR fbc-nuttx-esp32p4-firmware (1),
.BR nuttx-http-server (1),
.BR nuttx-remote-console (1)
.\"
.\" end of fbc-nuttx-esp32p4.1
